    "pathway_role_summary": "FZD1 is a critical Wnt receptor in canonical (beta-catenin-dependent) and non-canonical (PCP) Wnt signaling pathways. Upon binding Wnt ligands (WNT1/3/3A), FZD1 recruits LRP5/6 co-receptors and DVL proteins, leading to destruction complex disassembly, beta-catenin stabilization, and TCF/LEF-mediated transcription. FZD1 is negatively regulated by ZNRF3/RNF43 E3 ligases via ubiquitination and degradation. Dysregulation of FZD1 is implicated in cancer, neurodegeneration, and developmental disorders."
  },
