    "data_quality_notes": "Comprehensive data collected from multiple authoritative sources. Canonical sequence extracted from PDB structure 8J9N (579 residues shown in structure correspond to mature protein without signal peptide). Full 647 aa sequence includes signal peptide and N-terminal region. Specific phosphorylation sites not detailed in this digest but available in PhosphoSitePlus (Q9UP38). Ubiquitination sites not precisely mapped but ZNRF3/RNF43-mediated ubiquitination experimentally validated. Only one canonical isoform reported in major databases. Disulfide bond pattern critical for CRD structure and Wnt binding.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "FZD1 is a critical node in Wnt signaling networks essential for modeling canonical and non-canonical Wnt pathways. Key features for signaling models: (1) Wnt ligand selectivity (WNT1/3/3A high affinity); (2) LRP5/6 co-receptor requirement; (3) DVL recruitment via C-terminal PDZ motif; (4) ZNRF3/RNF43-mediated degradation as negative feedback; (5) Tissue-specific expression patterns; (6) Disease relevance in cancer and development. Cryo-EM structures (8J9O, 8J9N) provide structural basis for active/inactive states and G protein coupling. Critical for modeling Wnt pathway activation, signal amplification, receptor turnover, and pathway crosstalk with Hippo and mTOR signaling."
  }
